; The relative bound needs the root class to stay off zero, which the full box
; cannot show: -b + sqrt(b*b-d) > 0 whenever d < 0, but the interval straddles.
; The subtraction's condition number is unbounded, so it gets a guarded node.
; SameSign(sqrt(b*b-d), b) rewrites to b > 0 because the root is positive, and
; in the b > 0 context sqrt(b*b-d) + b is provably nonzero -- which fires the
; conjugate rule there and nowhere else.
(FPCore (b d)
  :name "guarded conjugate"
  :pre (and (<= -10 b 10) (<= -2 d -1))
  (+ (- b) (sqrt (- (* b b) d))))
